      "writtenOn": "2024-10-01T04:57:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nicely readable, though i don\u0027t love that this might have do hundreds of modulus ops (up to rate-6 i believe). The correct code that only uses a single modulus doesn\u0027t seem _that_ bad to me:\n\n```\nif padlen :\u003d rate - len(out)%rate; padlen \u003c rate {\n    out \u003d append(out, make([]byte, padlen)...)\n}\n```\n\n(I wish go had ceiling div and ceiling mod operations, but that\u0027s a topic for another time)\n\nAs an additional optimization, we don\u0027t even have to append zeros - the tail of the buffer is already zeroed and large enough to slice it to [:len(out)+padlen]",
      "revId": "b63376a92f7929fc9c1b5f53f354a484f7a91adf",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ef9fdee_3594a6db",
        "filename": "sha3/shake.go",
